Web Application Automation Testing – Selenium with Java
Project Overview
This is a self-directed web application automation testing project developed using Selenium WebDriver and Java.
The project focuses on automating important web application scenarios and demonstrates practical knowledge of Selenium WebDriver, Java programming, web element identification, XPath, explicit waits, TestNG, and Page Object Model.
Objectives
•	Automate common web application workflows
•	Practice Selenium WebDriver with Java
•	Implement reliable element identification and synchronization
•	Apply Java OOP concepts in test automation
•	Develop maintainable automation scripts
•	Document test scenarios, test cases, and defects
•	Maintain the project using Git and GitHub
